<!--
  GLOA sitemap.

  There was none: /sitemap.xml fell through to the catch-all and
  answered HTTP 200 with the site's HTML.

  This lists exactly the URLs in INDEXABLE_ROUTES (lib/publicRoutes.ts),
  in the same order, and tests/seo-discovery.test.mjs fails if the two
  ever disagree - so a page added to the site cannot silently go missing
  here, and a URL cannot appear here without existing.

  DELIBERATELY ABSENT:
    /account/*, /auth/*, /order/*   private or transactional
    /rezepte, /journal              withheld for this launch
    /shop/metal-case                not a launch product
    /wholesale                      alias; /for-cafes is canonical
    /adminxyzuebersicht             not public

  No <lastmod>, <changefreq> or <priority>. A lastmod that is not
  maintained is worse than none - it teaches a crawler to distrust the
  file - and changefreq/priority are hints search engines have long
  ignored. Omitting them is valid sitemap XML and states nothing false.
-->
